From: Andrea Pesaresi <andreapesaresi82@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 11:58:07 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] ksmbd: fix SMB1 negotiate header layout

The linux-6.18.y backport of commit 0a70cac78967 ("ksmbd: Fix to
handle removal of rfc1002 header from smb_hdr") changed the SMB1
negotiate paths to use smb_get_msg().  This helper skips the four-byte
RFC1002 header before casting the message to struct smb_hdr.

Unlike mainline, linux-6.18.y still keeps the RFC1002 length field in
ksmbd's private struct smb_hdr.  The field is therefore skipped twice,
which shifts the SMB1 request and response fields by four bytes and
breaks Windows multi-protocol negotiation.

Remove the stale field so that struct smb_hdr describes the message
returned by smb_get_msg(), matching the layout expected by the
backported negotiation and minimum-PDU-size changes.

Fixes: 29dbb4e29e1f ("ksmbd: Fix to handle removal of rfc1002 header from smb_hdr")
Signed-off-by: Andrea Pesaresi <andreapesaresi82@gmail.com>
---
 fs/smb/server/smb_common.h | 1 -
 1 file changed, 1 deletion(-)

--- a/fs/smb/server/smb_common.h
+++ b/fs/smb/server/smb_common.h
@@ -163,7 +163,6 @@
 #define SMBFLG2_UNICODE		cpu_to_le16(0x8000)
 
 struct smb_hdr {
-	__be32 smb_buf_length;
 	__u8 Protocol[4];
 	__u8 Command;
 	union {
